# Game content, downloaded by `arc_agi`'s NORMAL mode into `environments_dir`.
# BEFORE THE FIRST DOWNLOAD, WHICH IS THE ONLY TIME IT IS FREE. This repo is public and the
# files are not ours to redistribute -- and the second firewall's real work starts here: the
# seat may read them, the agent may read only the frame.
environment_files/
recordings/

# PROTOCOL run traces -- one ledger dump per (batch, board, depth), ~1MB each.
# Written by scratchpad/protocol.py so a finding can be re-read without re-running.
# They are RUN OUTPUT, not source: regenerable, large, and `runs/` is already ignored
# for the same reason. Kept out of the repo root's sight rather than deleted, because
# F75/F76 cite them by name.
protocol_*.jsonl

# Human-panel replays -- the ANSWER SET (arcprize.org/replay/<uuid>): jsonl + gif per game.
# Out of git (large, not ours to redistribute) AND out of the agent's reach -- the seat reads
# the answer set, the agent reads only the frame. Same firewall as environment_files/.
replays/
out/
